TEXT 32 232 Left 2 ;If the transformer is a three limb (rkessel 1e5-1e6) or a five limb core type\nwith compensating third winding there is also a\nsmall additional displacement voltage at the star point of the secondary\nside if earth fault on the primary side occur\nThis is because of the assymetrie of the secondary voltages\nThis is even more true at transformers with 5 limbs core\nor 3x1 transformer cores where the displacement voltage\ncan reach the full phase voltage (like on the primary side)\nTherefore it seems also not a good idea if both sides\nof a Yy transformer are grounded by petersen coils\nNOTE: It should work only by a five leg 9limbs core with additional delta winding\nIt work in princip also on a 3leg core but all assymetrics goes through rkessel
TEXT -160 144 Left 2 ;Switching at 505ms gives highest current !!
